type: software
title: "quantum-linear-rank-cone: Data, certificates and code for stabilizer entropy cones"
version: R47
date-released: 2026-10-20
authors:
  - family-names: Cao
    given-names: Ruifeng
    affiliation: "School of Engineering, The University of Manchester"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9077-9561"
  - family-names: Song
    given-names: Xidan
    affiliation: "School of Computer Science, Wuhan University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2612-6296"
repository-code: "https://github.com/RuifengCao/quantum-linear-rank-cone"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Exact data, certificates and code for stabilizer entropy cones: the five-party
  quantum linear rank cone and a catalog of its extreme rays, exact certificates
  that separate the five-party stabilizer entropy cone from it, graph-state
  realizations of extreme rays, the dependence of stabilizer entropy cones on the
  local dimension, bounds on the information ratio of stabilizer quantum secret
  sharing schemes, a self-test suite of verification gates, and the verification
  scripts (directory checks) of the paper "Stabilizer entropy cones as self-dual
  slices of linear rank cones: a five-party gap and dependence on the local
  dimension" by X. Song and R. Cao (arXiv:2610.18905). The code is under the MIT license, the data
  (directories data and results) are under the CC BY 4.0 license, and bin/normaliz
  is an unmodified binary of Normaliz under its own license (GPL-3).
keywords:
  - stabilizer states
  - entropy cones
  - linear rank inequalities
  - matroids
  - quantum information
